# %% [markdown]
# # First experiment —PCA and temporal CNN
#
# This script is the second step of the first NeuroBridge experiment.
#
# It loads the synthetic multi-subject simulation generated by
# ``First_experiment_24_07.py`` and asks a controlled representation-learning
# question:
#
#     How well can a linear method (PCA) and a nonlinear temporal encoder
#     (TemporalCNNEncoder) recover the known latent structure from neural
#     population activity?
#
# PCA and CNN receive exactly the same centered temporal windows. PCA flattens
# each window, whereas the CNN preserves its temporal structure. Both methods
# are evaluated against:
# The only latent benchmark used in this file is ``Z_task``.
#
# ``Z_task`` is the shared task-level latent trajectory that we want to
# recover from the simulated neural population activity.
#
# This first analysis uses all available windows. It is a descriptive
# latent-recovery experiment, not yet an out-of-sample decoding experiment.


